flupdate -- the update notifier
===============================

flupdate-notify is a small shell daemon the desktop session starts
(src/flcomp/session). Five minutes after login, then once a day, it runs

    flpkg check-updates                       the FreeLFS package repo (D3)
    flatpak remote-ls --updates --user        Flathub, the person's own apps

and posts one notification, "N updates available" (body: how many system
packages and Flatpak apps), through org.freedesktop.Notifications (flnotify;
the panel is the daemon). The next check replaces the card. Clicking the card
or its "Open Store" button runs `flstore --updates`. It only tells; it never
installs or syncs anything system-wide. flpkg downloads the signed index to a
temporary directory and needs no root. A failed check (offline, no repo) posts
nothing and is retried after an hour. It refuses to run as root.

Environment: FLUPDATE_FIRST (300 s), FLUPDATE_INTERVAL (86400 s),
FLUPDATE_RETRY (3600 s); --once checks now and exits. FLUPDATE_FLPKG,
FLUPDATE_FLATPAK, FLUPDATE_FLNOTIFY, FLUPDATE_STORE name other programs (tests).

Test: `make check` (tests/notify.sh) runs it against made-up flpkg, flatpak,
flnotify and flstore programs: no network, no bus, no root.
